We thank the reviewer for finding our paper "well-written" and our method "novel and interesting". Below is our feedback on the questions.

&nbsp;

**R4-Q1: more training details?**

Thanks for the suggestion. We fully agree that showing the training details in the main paper is important. We have moved the training details to Section 4 *implementation details* in the revised paper from Appendix.  

&nbsp;

**R4-Q2: comparing more methods in Table 2?**

Thanks for the suggestion. We have added the results of (Hou et al., 2019) and iCaRL (Rebuffi et al., 2017) to Table 2 in the revised paper.

&nbsp;

**R4-Q3: more visualization results?**

Thanks for the suggestion. We will provide more visualization results for different classes (like Figure 3(a)) in our final version.

&nbsp;

**R4-Q4: more recent related papers?**

We have added this related work (ELI) to Table 2 in the revised paper. We can observe that our method consistently outperforms it on two datasets (CIFAR-100 and ImageNet-100), e.g. improving the average accuracy of the $N=5$ setting by $3.19$ and $8.49$ percentage points on CIFAR-100 and ImageNet-100, respectively.
